  "metadata": {
    "title": "Confiança Verificável para Trading Quantitativo Multi-Mercado e Multi-Domínio: A Arquitetura em Nove Camadas do Arkhe OS, sua Implementação Descentralizada e sua Fundamentação Bioinspirada",
    "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.22774038",
    "publication_date": "2026-09-15",
    "description": "<p>Institutional allocation of capital to AI-agent-driven strategies faces a structural trust deficit: the execution chain &mdash;<br>from the data feeding the model to the bytes signing the order &mdash; remains largely unverifiable. This paper develops<br>and consolidates the Arkhe OS architecture, a transversal verification layer for multi-market, multi-domain<br>quantitative trading, organized into nine layers (agent attestation; economic, geopolitical, scientific-technological<br>and sociocultural data; verification and oraclization; markets; governance; and institutional reporting), such that each<br>layer integrates one data domain and is covered by a dedicated verification component. Through documentary<br>analysis with external source verification (30+ queries, accessed 15 September 2026), the paper examines: the fully<br>decentralized implementation plan, which removes single points of failure via DNSLink/IPFS, Merkle-root content<br>addressing on Nostr (Hashtree), non-profit code hosting (Codeberg/Forgejo), 4-of-7 or 5-of-7 threshold multisig<br>custody (Safe) and distributed key validation (SSV); the bioinspired grounding of its invariants, from controlled<br>plasticity to detection under noise and oxidative eustress as a metaphor for honest verification status; and the<br>implementation gaps (estimated 46&ndash;62 weeks). Counterarguments &mdash; verification latency, the distance between<br>attestation and stochastic behavior, decentralization trade-offs and methodological limitations &mdash; are discussed,<br>concluding that the proposal constitutes a plausible auditable market-intelligence stack, contingent on future<br>empirical evaluation.</p>",
